Subject: [PATCH 4/4] media: i2c: ov13b10: restore the OF match table

The ov13b10 driver of this tree only carries an ACPI match table, so a
sensor described in the device tree can never bind. The i2c core matches
an OF device through the driver of_match_table, and there is none here.

On the lmi board the rear sensor node (compatible "ovti,ov13b10") is
therefore created by the core but never probed: the driver registers, the
i2c client exists with the right modalias, and nothing happens. No probe
message, no subdev, no /dev/v4l-subdev node, only the ISP outputs of the
camss device.

Restore the OF match table for the two upstream compatible strings and
declare it in the driver. The ACPI table and the ACPI behaviour are left
untouched, so the platforms this rework targeted keep working.

No device tree change is needed for this board: the rear sensor node
already carries one 19.2 MHz clock, which is OV13B10_EXT_CLK, the avdd,
dovdd and dvdd supplies, a reset gpio, four CSI-2 data lanes and a
560 MHz link frequency, which is what the driver checks.

Generated for the lmi Linux 7.2.12 camera bring-up; the same patch
applies to the pinned tree used by the observer kit, where the observer
device tree describes no sensor and the change is inert.
---
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov13b10.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov13b10.c
@@ -1705,10 +1705,18 @@
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(acpi, ov13b10_acpi_ids);
 #endif
 
+static const struct of_device_id ov13b10_of_match[] = {
+	{ .compatible = "ovti,ov13b10" },
+	{ .compatible = "ovti,ov13b10r" },
+	{ /* sentinel */ }
+};
+MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, ov13b10_of_match);
+
 static struct i2c_driver ov13b10_i2c_driver = {
 	.driver = {
 		.name = "ov13b10",
 		.pm = pm_ptr(&ov13b10_pm_ops),
+		.of_match_table = ov13b10_of_match,
 		.acpi_match_table = ACPI_PTR(ov13b10_acpi_ids),
 	},
 	.probe = ov13b10_probe,
